1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,820
Khabardar. It means beware.

2
00:00:02,820 --> 00:00:04,000
Flood warnings for your house

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:05,180
not your district.

4
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:08,120
In 2022

5
00:00:08,120 --> 00:00:11,400
one monsoon put a third of Pakistan under water.

6
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:13,840
Thirty-three million people were affected.

7
00:00:13,840 --> 00:00:16,900
The warnings that existed named whole districts.

8
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:18,880
But water doesn't flood a district.

9
00:00:18,880 --> 00:00:20,220
It floods a house.

10
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:23,160
Here is how it works.

11
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:26,320
Move the pin anywhere in Pakistan and tap once.

12
00:00:26,320 --> 00:00:28,300
It checks the river forecast

13
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:30,800
heavy rain, and flash floods in the hills

14
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:33,440
and gives one answer for the next seven days.

15
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:36,900
This is Dadu in 3D

16
00:00:36,900 --> 00:00:39,740
on the twenty-seventh of August 2022

17
00:00:39,740 --> 00:00:42,080
the day the Johi channel peaked.

18
00:00:42,080 --> 00:00:45,300
The blue is what satellites saw under water.

19
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:48,060
Every house is coloured by its own risk.

20
00:00:49,100 --> 00:00:50,940
In Nowshera and Dadu

21
00:00:50,940 --> 00:00:54,200
all forty-four thousand houses have their own level.

22
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:55,740
Here is one near Johi

23
00:00:55,740 --> 00:00:58,840
on the twenty-fifth of August 2022.

24
00:00:58,840 --> 00:01:00,660
Danger, from the twenty-seventh.

25
00:01:00,660 --> 00:01:02,260
Three meters above the river

26
00:01:02,260 --> 00:01:03,640
and it flooded before.

27
00:01:04,700 --> 00:01:06,420
And the warning is spoken

28
00:01:06,420 --> 00:01:07,780
in Urdu, Sindhi

29
00:01:07,780 --> 00:01:09,260
Punjabi or English.

30
00:01:13,700 --> 00:01:14,980
Does it work?

31
00:01:14,980 --> 00:01:17,720
We replayed the real 2022 flood.

32
00:01:17,720 --> 00:01:19,760
The Johi channel crossed our warning line

33
00:01:19,760 --> 00:01:22,300
ten days before its record peak.

34
00:01:22,300 --> 00:01:25,180
Blue houses are the ones that really went under.

35
00:01:25,180 --> 00:01:27,040
Johi town stayed dry.

36
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:30,740
We also show where it falls short.

37
00:01:30,740 --> 00:01:33,500
At Nowshera, Pakistan's own gauges saw five

38
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:36,280
times more water than the free global model.

39
00:01:36,280 --> 00:01:37,600
The timing was right

40
00:01:37,600 --> 00:01:39,400
the size was not.

41
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:41,460
Adding those gauges is our next step.

42
00:01:42,300 --> 00:01:45,080
And we tested every house blind.

43
00:01:45,080 --> 00:01:47,300
The houses we flag really flooded seventy

44
00:01:47,300 --> 00:01:48,860
-six percent of the time

45
00:01:48,860 --> 00:01:50,980
against forty-six for the rest.

46
00:01:52,520 --> 00:01:54,020
Khabardar. Free data

47
00:01:54,020 --> 00:01:55,400
every house in Pakistan

48
00:01:55,400 --> 00:01:56,780
in your own language.
